[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-001-security.md#53-merge-and-spread-restrictions]

### 5.3 Merge and Spread Restrictions

- JSON schema validation **must** be performed before any `Object.assign()` or object spread (`{...source}`) operation on user-supplied data.
- The key `__proto__` must be explicitly rejected in all parsed JSON input. Configure the JSON body parser to reject payloads containing `__proto__` or `constructor.prototype`:

```typescript
import express from 'express';

app.use(
  express.json({
    limit: '1mb',
    reviver: (_key, value) => {
      if (_key === '__proto__' || _key === 'constructor' || _key === 'prototype') {
        return undefined;
      }
      return value;
    },
  })
);
```

