[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-001-security.md#71-prohibited-patterns]

### 7.1 Prohibited Patterns

The following are prohibited when any portion of the command or arguments originates from user input or external data:

```typescript
// PROHIBITED — shell interpolation of user input
import { exec } from 'child_process';
exec(`convert ${req.body.filename} output.pdf`);

// PROHIBITED — string-form setTimeout/setInterval
setTimeout('doSomething()', 1000);
```

These patterns are enforced by ESLint rules in STD-TEC-NODE-002.

