[standards/technology/nodejs/STD-TEC-NODE-001-security.md#82-per-request-timeout-budgets]

### 8.2 Per-Request Timeout Budgets

All outbound HTTP calls (upstream APIs, third-party integrations) **must** have an explicit timeout. Use `AbortController` with `fetch` or the `timeout` option on HTTP client libraries:

```typescript
import { setTimeout as setTimeoutPromise } from 'timers/promises';

async function fetchWithTimeout(url: string, timeoutMs: number): Promise<Response> {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), timeoutMs);
  try {
    return await fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal });
  } finally {
    clearTimeout(timeoutId);
  }
}
```

